al event timestamps along candidate intermediaries were not enumerated.", "confidence": 0.5}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_049448d4\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [767, 1635],\n  \"window\": [20674, 59073],\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Within the interval, node 767 emits to only three targets (722, 988, 1719) [step_03], while node 1635 receives from only three sources (106, 133, 302) [step_02]. These sets are disjoint, so any influence path from 767 to 1635 needs at least three hops, and the observable out-edges of 767's targets point back toward hubs (e.g. 302->722, 133->722 in the k-hop structure of step_01) rather than onward to 1635's in-neighbours, so no short forward chain is visible. The activity that does exist is spread thinly and fairly uniformly across the 38k-unit span (4-23 events per 2.4k-unit bucket for the whole node set, step_04), which makes it implausible that consecutive hops of such a chain fall within the required 600-unit gaps; the mere existence of a time-ignoring connection in the 2-hop neighbourhood (step_01) and the general volume of activity (step_04) are therefore treated as confounders rather than support. Conclusion: no genuine time-respecting cascade from 767 to 1635; confidence is moderate because individual event timestamps along candidate intermediaries were not enumerated.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 17742, "total_output_tokens": 4483, "total_tokens": 22225, "total_latency_ms": 68326, "llm_calls": 4, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}